		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=41654#p41654"><![CDATA[
PyBullet doesn't use constraints by default, it uses btMultiBody primarily. So joints are not represented by constraints internally.<br><div class="codebox"><p>Code: </p><pre><code>then create a constraint that encapsulates those DOFs without having to do collision detection/simulation</code></pre></div>Why? Can you explain more in detail what you try to do with PyBullet on a higher level?<br><br>There is a UrdfEditor, that let's you build more complex constructions in Python and then instantiate it in PyBullet.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2">Erwin Coumans</a> — Fri Nov 30, 2018 6:03 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
